Font
----

Liberation Sans 2.1.5: SIL Open Font License 1.1
Digitized data copyright (c) 2010 Google Corporation, with Reserved Font Names Arimo, Tinos and Cousine;
copyright (c) 2012 Red Hat, Inc., with Reserved Font Name Liberation.

    static/fonts/liberation-sans/LiberationSans-Regular.ttf and LiberationSans-Bold.ttf, shipped unmodified with
    upstream's licence (OFL.txt), AUTHORS and ChangeLog. The sheet is drawn in Liberation Sans only when an address
    uses letters the built-in Helvetica lacks (Welsh, Polish, Turkish and similar); the fonts are then fetched from this
    site and embedded into the PDF as a subset by the fontkit library above. Source: the Liberation Fonts project's
    release tarball liberation-fonts-ttf-2.1.5.tar.gz, sha256 7191c669bf38899f73a2094ed00f7b800553364f90e2637010a69c0e268f25d0.

Icons and marks
---------------

The interface icons (delete, save, print, history, close) are Material Symbols (Google, Apache-2.0): each is a single
path from @material-symbols/svg-400, inlined into the page as SVG. Nothing is fetched at runtime.

The CaseForge name, the anvil mark and the favicon are CaseForge's, used to say who made the tool. They are not
covered by the licence of the code: do not use them to suggest that your own copy comes from CaseForge.
